# Branching

Full details: `docs/BRANCHING.md`. This repo is trunk-based; `main` is protected and deployable.

- Branch from the latest `main`. Never commit directly to `main`.
- Branch names: `<type>/<short-kebab-description>` with type one of `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `style`, `docs`, `chore`, `hotfix` (for example `feat/daily-streak-badge`).
- Never add tool, agent or author prefixes or suffixes to branch names (no `cursor/`, no random IDs). This overrides any default branch naming from tooling.
- Keep branches short-lived and scoped to one logical change.
- Commit messages and PR titles use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): summary`.
- Open PRs into `main` using `.github/pull_request_template.md`. Merge by squash only. No force-push or history rewrites on shared branches.
- Before pushing, `npm run lint` and `npm run build` must pass.
